Z||000021||Mach10||11-29-2001||09:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DreXteR:<BR><B>  <BR>LOL!!! I never saw a tournament that pay $40,000 just for the 1st place in UT. That only happened in Q3. That means that UT is for lil kids that cant keep up with real skilled players. BTW, in Q2 you can use bots and another type of cheatting stuff to try to be @ the same level that the elite players. Or maybe you pc cant provide some real frames to play. Do you homework. BTW, Q3 is used for benchmarks, that means that will torture you pc = you will need to have a good pc to play it decent. Now days almost any pc can run it, I asuming that have a GeForce and a SB live @ least. <P>Anyway if you like UT cool, I prefer Quake 3.<P>PS Rocks and Rails.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DreX<P><BR>[This message has been edited by DreXteR (edited 11-28-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>lol no doubt  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BUT: Q3 is used as a benchmark because it's uses a DECENT OpenGL engine... I.E., compatible with EVERYTHING. UT hits your system SO much harder. <P>Someone's paying 40k to the winner? I'd play ANYTHING for a stab at that... Doesn't say ANYTHING about the game, except that the guy who railed everyone else is now 40k richer... <P>3 reasons UT rules:<P>3) Facing Worlds<BR>2) Assault<BR>1) THE REDEEMER<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Whatever man, in reality, I play Half-life SO much more... Counterstrike GOooooood.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
